{
  "requirement": "For a Cargo workspace that depends on `habeas`, interactive `cargo agents sync` MUST let the user enable Habeas's plugin. Once enabled, it MUST make the skills shipped with the selected Habeas version available to configured agents. After the selected version changes, `cargo agents sync` MUST provide the skills shipped with the new version.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** `requirements.integration.symposium` is met. The implementation is complete and marked, and the test covers each obligation.\n\n**Implementation (`Cargo.toml`, all marked `{impl}`):**\n- `[package.metadata.symposium] name = \"habeas\"` (lines 14–15) declares Habeas's Symposium plugin for any workspace that depends on `habeas`.\n- `[package.metadata.symposium.defaults] skills = false` (lines 18–19) keeps the skills off until the user chooses to enable the plugin. That fits the \"let the user enable\" obligation.\n- `[[package.metadata.symposium.skills]] source.path = \"assets/skills\"` (lines 22–23) points Symposium at the skills shipped inside the crate. `assets/skills` exists and holds three skill directories: `habeas-bootstrap-requirements`, `habeas-evidence` and `habeas-requirements`.\n- Because the skills ship inside the crate, they track the selected Habeas version. `Cargo.toml` has no `include` or `exclude` that would drop them from the package.\n- The other `symposium` tables (installations and hooks) are marked for `symposium_cli` and `symposium_setup_hook`, not for this requirement. No unspecified behaviour is attributed to this requirement.\n\n**Test (`tests/symposium_hook_smoke.py`, `{test}` at line 203 in `main`):**\n- It runs a real `cargo agents sync` on a pty via `interactive_sync`. It waits for the \"Enable it?\" prompt and selects the non-default option. It then checks that the decision was saved to the config. This covers the interactive-enable obligation.\n- It checks that every skill directory under the repo's `assets/skills` is installed byte-for-byte under `.agents/skills`. This covers the obligation that enabling makes the shipped skills available to configured agents.\n- It then builds a \"next\" crate: version bumped, one skill changed, repointed as the consumer's `habeas` dependency. A plain `symposium sync` must replace the installed skill with the new content. This covers the version-change obligation.\n- CI runs the test in the `symposium-hook` job in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, with Symposium 0.5.1 pinned.\n\n**Gaps:** None found. The test is a heavyweight smoke test that needs `cargo-agents`. That fits an integration with an external tool, and it is wired into CI.",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.integration.symposium",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.integration.symposium"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} symposium",
        "For a Cargo workspace that depends on `habeas`, interactive `cargo agents sync` MUST let the user enable Habeas's plugin. Once enabled, it MUST make the skills shipped with the selected Habeas version available to configured agents. After the selected version changes, `cargo agents sync` MUST provide the skills shipped with the new version.",
        ":::"
      ]
